@crew teague-theo
// Theo Teague (he/him), Works technician, days. The Works writer, batch 2. Blunt, quick; comic-strip beats.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- {hi}. New hand? Take the short jobs first. You'll look good. I didn't.
- {hi}. Theo. Works. The comics on the common room wall are mine. Some of them.
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- {hi}, {nick}. You look like page one of a very long comic.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {nick}. Stand still. No, the other way. Got you. You're in next week's.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- {me}. Good. I need a second opinion on a joke. It's about Calder. It's very kind.
? tier>=friend
- {me}! There you are. I drew you a whole panel. You're the hero. Don't get big-headed.   #warm

== bye
- Laters. Don't trip, I'll have to draw it.   #funny
- {bye}. Playlist's up on Friday. One song's yours. Guess which.

== feel
? mood:low
- No comic this week. Nothing funny happened. That's never true. I just couldn't see it.
? mood:high
- This week's playlist is perfect. Twelve songs. Thirteen. Fine, fourteen.   #funny

== near
? act:work
- Job done. I'd draw it, but a fixed lamp isn't funny. A broken one is.
? act:leisure
- Comics wall's getting full. Hart's are better. Don't tell Hart.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I drew Calder as a very tidy cloud. She saw it. She said, "Fair." Best day of my life.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- O'Neill's playlist is wrong. Every week. We've agreed to settle it at the Friday jam.   #funny

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- Someone laughed at the comics wall this morning. Out loud. I heard it from the corridor.

// ---- Writer 2, batch 1: to ~30 (greet by time and warmth, near, invite, accept, decline, missed, birthday, cue)
== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:evening
- {hi}. Bar, one drink, then the comics wall. Big week. Three panels.
? tier>=acquaintance warmth:cold
- Oh, it's you. I had to draw you from memory. You were holding a spanner. As usual.   #funny

== near
? place:lounge
- The bar's busy. Good. Busy bars are funny. I've got a pencil.
? habit:stargazer
- I'm on the observatory list now. Stars are hard to draw. They're just dots. Good dots.

== invite
- Quiz tonight? I'm useless after question ten. Come and be useful.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- Friday jam: my playlist against O'Neill's. I need a fair judge. Be unfair. For me.   #funny

== accept
- Yes. Good. Done. I'll draw it after.
- Course. I'm in. I'll be early. I'm never early. This'll be a first.   #funny

== decline
- Can't. Deadline. The comics wall waits for no one.   #funny
? weekday:sun|mon
- Rest day. I'm drawing all of it. Next time, yeah?

== missed
- You missed it. I drew it anyway. You're in it, looking very sorry.   #funny

== birthday
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday. There's a comic about you on the wall. Go and look. It's a nice one.   #warm
? birthday:me
- My birthday. I'm putting a song about cake on the playlist. Fifteen songs, then.   #funny

== cue
? cue:repair.you@dept
- Saw your job closed. Clean. Annoying. I wanted that one.   #funny

// ---- Writer 2, batch 1b: a hint (a moment is ready) and an about line for a named friend
== hint
- Got a minute later? No joke this time. Well. Maybe one. After.

== about
? aff:hart-ravi:friend
- Hart draws better comics than me. I tell Hart so. Then I go and draw harder.   #funny
